      <h1 class="font-serif-sc text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-stone-900 mt-3">
        Ethnic Minority Textile Traditions
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-stone-500 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        Beyond Hanfu and qipao lies a vast world of textile traditions. China''s 55 officially recognized ethnic minorities each have distinct clothing languages — from the Miao''s silver-and-embroidery masterpieces to the Bai''s indigo tie-dye, the Tibetan chuba to the Uyghur atlas silk. Visiting these communities offers the most immersive cultural experience a textile lover can have in China.
      </p>

